    "description": "As part of an innovative platform project in the energy sector, we are seeking a Platform Operations Engineer (m/f/d) on behalf of our client. The role is primarily remote, with the option of traveling to Frankfurt or Berlin for a few days approximately once a month, by arrangement. Essentially, the Operations Engineer (m/f/d) is responsible for the stability, reliability, and continuous improvement of the containerized cloud infrastructure and DevOps toolchain. The DevOps Applications Team provides three products to the platform: CodeBuild (CI for automation and source management), Registry (Image and Artifact Registry), and the Developer Portal, which serves as a self-service hub for interacting with all products and other services. The goal is to streamline workflows on the platform by reducing overhead and automating tasks, allowing application developers to focus on business logic. Key Responsibilities: • Incident Management: Providing expert-level consultancy for critical incidents, root cause analysis, and advanced troubleshooting across production and staging environments • Carrying out SDLC-focused tasks: Maintaining and optimizing Kubernetes-based deployments, managing CI/CD pipelines, and ensuring the seamless operation of artifact repositories, security policies, and configuration management systems • Stakeholder Communication: Consulting with various stakeholders to ensure operational excellence and continuous delivery of high-quality software In essence, the Operations Engineer is responsible for the stability, reliability, and continuous improvement of containerized cloud infrastructure and DevOps toolchain. Objective: Guarantee operational stability Tasks: • Driving observability by leveraging the toolset provided by the Product Line • Focusing on advancing automation and being a consultant to internal stakeholders • Incorporating security best practices into daily business • Performing change management tasks and updating of software versions Objective: Process improvement Tasks: • Identifying and resolving performance bottlenecks proactively • Improving deployment processes to ensure smooth rollouts • Identifying gaps in processes and either improving already existing ones or setting up completely new processes Objective: Ensure availability of critical services Tasks: • Maintaining the integrity and performance of critical services • Being a consultant for internal stakeholders on complex operational challenges • Communicating with external stakeholders regarding incidents and overseeing them end-to-end Profile Requirements DevOps Engineer (m/f/d) with experience in the operational part of DevOps, process analysis and optimization as well as change management. Must-have experience • Hands-on experience and operational knowledge in deployment tools Preferred tools: Harbor, Opentofu Controller, Kyverno-Operator, ArgoCD • Hands-on experience in maintaining and operating Git and CI tools Preferred tools: Gitlab, Harness • Experience in using Planning, Documentation and Management tools Preferred tools: Jira Service Management, Jira, Confluence • Strong experience in Kubernetes, DevOps automation, and cloud-native ecosystems with a deep knowledge of Helm, Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC), and GitOps principles • Knowledge in Linux administration, scripting (eg, Bash, Python, Go), and observability tools • Proven experience in Operations, SRE, or DevOps, ideally within enterprise-scale or multi-cluster environments Must-have language skills: • Fluent English in speech and writing (at least C1) Preferred experience • Knowledge of CI/CD tools (eg FluxCD), backup and restore tools (eg Velero), artifactory tools (eg JFrog Artifactory) and developer platform tools (eg Backstage) • Operational and administrative knowledge about Planning, Documentation and Management tools (eg Jira Service Management, Jira, Confluence\n\nSkills: DevOps, Kubernetes, helmet, Linux, Git, Continuous Delivery, Continuous Integration",
